# Python style rules

- Keep `from __future__ import annotations` in modules that use modern annotations.
- Prefer dataclasses with `frozen=True, slots=True` for immutable domain values.
- Prefer `Mapping` for read-only inputs.
- Use `MappingProxyType` when storing immutable mapping views makes sense.
- Use Python 3.12 generic syntax where this repo already uses it.
- Use typed enum IDs for public identifiers.
- Avoid raw strings in public track/spec/entity APIs except in generic tests.
- Use clear function names instead of comments that repeat the function name.
- Keep module docstrings useful and high-level. Do not narrate every line. The code is already there, doing its little performance.

## NumPy style

Canonical layout is time-major:

- `(T,)` for scalar/bool time series;
- `(T, 3)` for one vector signal;
- `(T, N, 3)` for multiple vector signals;
- `(T, 3, 3)` for rotation matrices.

Validate array shapes at construction boundaries.

Prefer `np.testing.assert_array_equal` / `assert_allclose` in tests.

